# AI-NIDS-Project

An enterprise-ready AI-powered Network Intrusion Detection System (NIDS) prototype built with:

- Go for high-performance packet capture and flow analysis
- Python for ML feature engineering and anomaly scoring
- Prometheus + Grafana for real-time monitoring and dashboarding
- REST API and SOC-style web dashboard for alert visualization
- Docker Compose for local deployment

The project demonstrates an end-to-end architecture for passive network traffic inspection using SPAN/mirror traffic, flow telemetry, AI-assisted anomaly scoring, and dashboard-based monitoring.

## Architecture overview

```text
Production traffic
       │
       ▼
[Core switch / SPAN port]
       │
       ▼
[Go capture agent]
       │  packet + flow metrics
       ▼
[ML scoring service]
       │  anomaly score + alert decisions
       ▼
[REST API]
       │
       ├── Grafana dashboard
       ├── Web SOC dashboard
       └── SIEM / alert log integration
```

## Current implementation

This repository now includes:

- a Go packet capture service for mirrored traffic ingestion
- a lightweight alert API for summary and incident retrieval
- a web dashboard for security monitoring
- a Prometheus/Grafana monitoring stack
- a sample network telemetry dataset and attack simulator
- ML training scaffolding for anomaly detection experiments

## Project structure

- `cmd/nids` — capture service entrypoint
- `cmd/api` — API service for alerts and summaries
- `internal/api` — alert server and response logic
- `python` — ML training and dataset tooling
- `dashboard` — Prometheus, Grafana, and web dashboard files
- `scripts` — setup automation
- `docker-compose.yml` — local environment bootstrap

## Quick start

### 1. Start the full stack

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

### 2. Access the dashboards

- Grafana: http://localhost:3000
- Web UI: http://localhost:8081
- Prometheus: http://localhost:9090
- API: http://localhost:8080/health

### 3. Set up Python environment and train the model

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r python/requirements.txt
python python/attack_simulator.py
python python/train_model.py
```

### 4. Run the packet capture service directly

```bash
go run ./cmd/nids --iface eth0
```

### 5. Run the API service directly

```bash
go run ./cmd/api
```

